From be130bf1b7acb66da7d840850b8ed1e10e20eb9d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xtu-v41 <xtu@local>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 23:18:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/16] feat(DSv4.1/SM80): portable Triton sparse-MLA prefill
 so V4.1 attention runs on A100

DeepSeek-V4.1 ships only FlashMLA (SM90+) and FlashInfer (SM100/SM120) attention.
On A100 `flash_mla_sparse_fwd` is a raise-stub, so the prefill path died. Add
`_forward_sparse_mla_prefill_triton`, which reuses the portable sparse-MLA kernels
we already built for DeepSeek-V4 (v1/attention/backends/mla/sparse_mla_kernels.py).

- only taken when `is_triton_sparse_mla_enabled(q.device)` (Ampere/Ada); the
  SM90+ `flash_mla_sparse_fwd` branch is untouched and byte-for-byte unchanged
- reserves the per-query softmax workspace in forward_mqa's warmup spec so the
  post-capture workspace stays large enough
- the surrounding machinery (dequantize_and_gather_k_cache,
  combine_topk_swa_indices) is unchanged; V4.1's KV format is fp8_ds_mla, the
  same as V4, so the gathered-KV contract matches

Verified on GPU 2 (A100, SM80) against a float32 torch reference
(gather rows by index, masked softmax over the first topk_length entries,
include the sink logit, weighted sum), deterministic over 3 runs:
  T=600 K=1536 H=64/128 D=512 R=2  max_abs=3.70e-3  max_rel=3.35e-2
  T=130 K=512  H=8/8   single chunk max_abs=1.95e-3  max_rel=1.51e-2
  T=37  K=200  H=16/64 padded heads max_abs=1.95e-3  max_rel=8.54e-3
  T=300 K=700  H=128/128 partial final topk chunk max_abs=3.01e-3 max_rel=3.18e-2
(errors are bf16 output rounding vs an fp32 reference.)

Note: decode still calls flash_mla_with_kvcache and is NOT yet ported.
(cherry picked from commit deb04fdd85d98104f83313874e1a55f0d1fd63ea)
